OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGYELTSIN ATTACKED BY
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGFORMER SUPPORTER
OL,5, A former supporter of Boris Yeltsin has
OL,6, accused the Russian leader of setting
OL,7, up a dictatorship and doing nothing to
OL,8, fix Russia's economic and social crisis
OL,10,FIn a scathing speech to the Russian
OL,11,FParliament, deputy Vladimir Isakov
OL,12,Faccused Mr Yeltsin and other radical
OL,13,Freformers of "democratic hysteria".
OL,14,F
OL,15,FMr Yeltsin, however, rejected claims he
OL,16,Fwas trying to break up the Soviet Union
OL,17,F
OL,18,FMr Yeltsin told deputies he had already
OL,19,Fput forward a number of proposals for
OL,20,Fstrengthening the union and signing the
OL,21,Funion treaty as soon as possible.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG30-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49605
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774910894
OL,1,Vk4                               G5/27
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGMANDELA MEETA INKATHA
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGCHIEF OVER VIOLENCE
OL,4,D
OL,5, A meeting between ANC leader Nelson
OL,6, Mandela and Chief Buthelezi of the
OL,7, Inkatha movement are meeting to discuss
OL,8, recent factional township violence.
OL,10,FThe Durban talks aim to find a way to
OL,11,Fend the fighting which flared up last
OL,12,FAugust and has spread to Johannesburg.
OL,14,FSince then, some 1,200 people have died
OL,15,Fin township fighting between Inkatha's
OL,16,FZulu followers and Xhosa supporters of
OL,17,Fthe African National Congress.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FOn his way to the talks, Mr Mandela
OL,20,Fsaid he was preparing an entirely new
OL,21,Fpeace initiative.
OL,23,D]FFromG30-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49606
