CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774910894
OL,1,Vk4                               G6/27
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGFIERCE FIGHTING IN
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGNORTHERN IRAQ
OL,4,D
OL,5, Fierce fighting is reported to be
OL,6, continuing in northern Iraq, with
OL,7, conflicting claims over who is in
OL,8, control of the oil city of Kirkuk.
OL,10,FKurdish rebels say they have retaken it
OL,11,Fafter an onslaught by government troops
OL,12,Fbriefly drove them out.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FBaghdad says its forces have regained
OL,15,FKirkuk and remain in control.
OL,17,FThe US state department confirmed that
OL,18,FIraqi troops seemed to be in control.
OL,19,F
OL,20,FReports say several oil fields were
OL,21,Fapparently set on fire during clashes.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG30-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49607
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774910894
OL,1,Vk4                               G7/27
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGKURDISH REBELS
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGAPPEAL TO UN
OL,4,D
OL,5, Kurdish rebels have appealed to the UN
OL,6, and the US-led coalition to intervene
OL,7, in the bitter fighting in northern Iraq
OL,9,FAfter claiming the recapture of Kirkuk,
OL,10,FKurdish forces said thousands of
OL,11,Fcivilians had been killed in reprisals
OL,12,Fby Saddam Hussein's troops.
OL,13,F
OL,14,F"What we are facing now is a campaign
OL,15,Fthat has all the hallmarks of genocide"
OL,16,Fsaid Kurdish leader Masoud Barzani.
OL,18,FThe US has reiterated that it would not
OL,19,Fintervene in fighting between Iraqi
OL,20,Ffactions, saying it had no mandate from
OL,21,Fthe United Nations to do so.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG30-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49608
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774910894
OL,1,Vk4                               G8/27
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGGULF STATES TO CUT AID
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGTO JORDAN & PLO
OL,4,D
OL,5, The Gulf Cooperation Council has said
OL,6, it is suspending aid to Jordan and the
OL,7, PLO because of their support for Iraq
OL,8, during the Gulf crisis.F
OL,10,FThe GCC represents six Arab nations and
OL,11,Fits secretary general Abdullah Beshara
OL,12,Fis a Kuwaiti.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FAnnouncing the move he said there could
OL,15,Fbe "no forgiveness, no forgetting".
OL,17,FHe said the GCC states - Saudi Arabia,
OL,18,FKuwait, Bahrain, Oman, Qatar and the
OL,19,FUnited Arab Emirates - could not
OL,20,Fsupport Amman and the PLO after they
OL,21,Fhad turned their backs on them.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG30-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49609
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774910894
OL,1,Vk4                               G9/27
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sG"ARROGANT POLITICIANS
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGEXPLOIT CHILDREN"
OL,4,D
OL,5, The newly elected president of the
OL,6, National Union of Teachers has accused
OL,7, "arrogant and ignorant" politicians of
OL,8, exploiting staff and pupils.
OL,10,FAnne Morgan said that children were
OL,11,Fsuffering from being used as an
OL,12,Fexperiment for the Education Reform Act
OL,14,FShe told delegates at the union's
OL,15,Fnational conference in Scarborough it
OL,16,Fwas a miracle that schools were
OL,17,Fsurviving the Act.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FMeanwhile, union members will decide
OL,20,Ftoday whether to boycott new tests for
OL,21,Fseven-year-olds
OL,23,D]FFromG30-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
